      heading: 'How do you choose everyday words in Talk+?',
      paragraphs: ['The app includes more than 1,000 words across 25 themes. This offers variety, not a checklist every child must finish. Choose a small set connected to what is happening: food for snack time, animals for a story or actions for a game.', 'Pictures and voice present content within an activity. Recognising a game picture does not prove a word will be used spontaneously elsewhere. To explore that connection, return to the actual object or experience and welcome gestures, pointing and picture choices too.'],
      steps: ['Pick a theme that connects with the day’s routine.', 'Explore a few words in an accessible activity without requesting repetition after every picture.', 'Return to one word during real play, reading or a familiar routine.'],
      example: 'After finding an apple in a game, look at a real apple: its colour, skin and what you can do with it. You might say “red apple” or “cut the apple”, depending on the situation. Snack time need not become a series of questions. Aim to open up conversation and participation.',
