      lead: 'The <strong>Talk+ weekly report</strong> brings usage records into a PDF that adults can share. It offers concrete information about app experiences for conversations with families, schools and professionals.',
      heading: 'How should you interpret the Talk+ weekly report?',
      paragraphs: ['The weekly technical report is a Premium feature. Time, activities and responses describe what happened within the app. They are not a clinical report, standardised test or overall measure of a child’s development.', 'Before comparing weeks, check whether games, levels, available time or adult assistance changed. More correct answers in a familiar game and fewer in a new challenge may reflect different contexts. A break from the app should not automatically be interpreted as lost skills.'],
      steps: ['Open the report in the Adult Area and check the profile and period.', 'Read records alongside context: company, help and selected activities.', 'Share the PDF only with appropriate recipients and ask a concrete question.'],
